{
  "assessment": "The source provides a complete theoretical model for heat transport in a chain of M Coulomb islands with N chiral ballistic channels in the Heat Coulomb Blockade regime. It derives the temperature profile, heat flow, and Lorenz ratio, with explicit formulas for the large-chain limit. The key quantitative cluster is the Lorenz ratio as a function of chain length M and channel number N, with the central formula L ≈ sqrt((N-1)(M+1))/N * L0. This supports a numeric control (M, N), a numeric readout (Lorenz ratio), a quantitative mechanism (the heat diffusion equation and its solution), and an objective response within an explicit domain (M >> N). The source also provides specific parameter values (L0, kappa0, G0) and fixed conditions (T_S=35 mK, T_D=15 mK). The extraction is case_authoring_ready.",
  "case_authoring_ready": true,
  "source": {
    "citation": "Patrice Roche, Breakdown of the Wiedemann-Franz Law in an Interacting Quantum Hall Metamaterial, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/twbt-z82z",
    "journal_doi": "10.1103/twbt-z82z",
    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2510.10391v3"
  },
  "paper_scope": "The paper theoretically analyzes heat transport through a 1D chain of M Coulomb islands connected by N chiral ballistic edge channels in the integer quantum Hall regime, focusing on the Heat Coulomb Blockade (HCB) regime where charge dynamics are frozen. It derives the temperature profile, heat flow, and Lorenz ratio, showing a violation of the Wiedemann-Franz law with the Lorenz ratio scaling as sqrt(M) for N>1. The main quantitative results are the heat diffusion equation, the approximate temperature profile, the heat flow formula, and the Lorenz ratio formula in the large-chain limit.",
  "mechanisms": [
    {
      "mechanism_id": "heat_diffusion_equation",
      "statement": "The temperature profile of the chain is governed by a discrete diffusion equation balancing local diffusion by neutral modes (LN/RN) and a non-local equalizing term from the split neutral (SN) mode. The equation is (N-1)[T_{k+1}^2 - 2T_k^2 + T_{k-1}^2] = 4(T_k^2 - T_mid^2)/(M+1), with T_mid^2 = (T_S^2 + T_D^2)/2. The decay length is Delta = sqrt((N-1)(M+1))/2.",
      "equations": [
        "(N-1)[T_{k+1}^2 - 2T_k^2 + T_{k-1}^2] = 4(T_k^2 - T_mid^2)/(M+1)",
        "Delta = sqrt((N-1)(M+1))/2"
      ],
      "variable_names": [
        "N",
        "M",
        "T_k",
        "T_mid",
        "Delta",
        "T_S",
        "T_D"
      ],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "T_mid_sq",
          "value": 0.000725,
          "uncertainty": "Not reported; computed from T_S=35 mK and T_D=15 mK as (T_S^2+T_D^2)/2.",
          "unit": "K^2",
          "role": "Mean squared temperature defined as (T_S^2+T_D^2)/2",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 100,
              "line_end": 102,
              "support": "T_mid^2=(T_S^2+T_D^2)/2 is defined in the diffusion equation context."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 97,
          "line_end": 102,
          "support": "The temperature profile is obtained from power balance, leading to the diffusion equation (N-1)[T_{k+1}^2-2T_k^2+T_{k-1}^2]=4(T_k^2-T_mid^2)/(M+1) with T_mid^2=(T_S^2+T_D^2)/2, and decay length Delta=sqrt((N-1)(M+1))/2."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "mechanism_id": "lorenz_ratio_scaling",
      "statement": "In the large chain limit M >> Delta (equivalently M >> N), the Lorenz ratio is approximately L = sqrt((N-1)(M+1))/N * L0, where L0 is the standard Lorenz number. This scaling holds for N>1 and M >> N.",
      "equations": [
        "L = sqrt((N-1)(M+1))/N * L0"
      ],
      "variable_names": [
        "L",
        "N",
        "M",
        "L0"
      ],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "L0",
          "value": 2.44e-08,
          "uncertainty": "Not reported; standard value.",
          "unit": "V^2/K^2",
          "role": "Standard Lorenz number L0 = pi^2 k_B^2 / (3 e^2)",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 44,
              "line_end": 44,
              "support": "L0 = pi^2 k_B^2 / (3 e^2) ≈ 2.44e-8 V^2/K^2 is stated."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 139,
          "line_end": 146,
          "support": "The Lorenz ratio is defined as L = [Qdot/(T_S-T_D)] / [G_el (T_S+T_D)/2] and in the large chain limit M >> Delta it approximates to sqrt((N-1)(M+1))/N * L0, scaling as sqrt(M)."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "fixed_conditions": [
    {
      "condition_id": "hc_regime",
      "statement": "The system is in the Heat Coulomb Blockade (HCB) regime where k_B T << hbar G_0 / C, so charge on each island is frozen and current noise cannot flow through the capacitance.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 64,
          "line_end": 64,
          "support": "In the HCB regime k_B T / hbar << G_0 / C, charge cannot vary on the island, so dq_k/dt = 0."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "condition_id": "source_drain_temps",
      "statement": "Source and drain temperatures are T_S = 35 mK and T_D = 15 mK, used in the figures and examples.",
      "anchors": [
